WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.275 --> 00:00:03.711
TO CALL BACK SOME OF THE

00:00:01.075 --> 00:00:05.346
EXECUTIVE POWER THAT HE HAS

00:00:03.845 --> 00:00:05.647
CEASED FOR HIMSELF IN RECENT

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.916
YEARS.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:08.583
&gt;&gt; Bret: A CONOR POWELL IN OUR

00:00:08.049 --> 00:00:09.751
MIDDLE EAST NEWSROOM.

00:00:08.716 --> 00:00:11.686
PLEASE JOIN ME SUNDAY NIGHT FOR

00:00:09.884 --> 00:00:13.221
A SPECIAL LOOK AT THE HISTORIC

00:00:11.819 --> 00:00:16.591
POINT IN TIME WHEN RONALD REAGAN

00:00:13.354 --> 00:00:17.525
BROUGHT THE MESSAGE OF PEACE AND

00:00:16.724 --> 00:00:18.126
FREEDOM TO WHAT WAS THEN THE

00:00:17.659 --> 00:00:20.528
SOVIET UNION.

00:00:18.259 --> 00:00:23.164
THE PROGRAM IS CALLED "THREE

00:00:20.662 --> 00:00:25.800
DAYS IN MOSCOW."

00:00:23.298 --> 00:00:27.569
IT'S BASED ON MY BOOK, AND HERE

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:28.770
IS A PREVIEW WITH THE MAN WHO

00:00:27.702 --> 00:00:32.540
SERVED AS THE PRESIDENT'S PRESS

00:00:28.903 --> 00:00:35.343
SECRETARY AT THE TIME.

00:00:32.674 --> 00:00:36.144
&gt;&gt; I GIVE A SPEECH AT MOSCOW

00:00:35.476 --> 00:00:38.279
UNIVERSITY WHERE THE PRESIDENT

00:00:36.277 --> 00:00:38.813
WANTED TO TALK ABOUT FREEDOM OF

00:00:38.613 --> 00:00:40.915
SPEECH.

00:00:38.947 --> 00:00:42.917
&gt;&gt; SET THE STAGE FOR THAT ONE.

00:00:41.049 --> 00:00:44.986
&gt;&gt; WHEN I WALKED IN THE DOOR, I

00:00:43.051 --> 00:00:47.155
WALKED INTO THE HEAD OF THE

00:00:45.119 --> 00:00:48.756
CHURCH WITH THIS HUGE STATUE OF

00:00:47.288 --> 00:00:50.391
LENIN AND A LECTERN WHICH WAS

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:51.626
SET UP FOR REAGAN WITH A LIGHT

00:00:50.525 --> 00:00:53.428
IN FRONT OF IT.

00:00:51.759 --> 00:00:53.861
&gt;&gt; YOU WERE THINKING IT WAS A

00:00:53.561 --> 00:00:57.398
BAD THING?

00:00:53.995 --> 00:00:57.966
&gt;&gt; I THINK IT WAS A HORRIBLE

00:00:57.532 --> 00:00:59.667
THING.

00:00:58.099 --> 00:01:05.106
BUT PRESIDENT REAGAN SAW IT AS

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:06.107
AN OPPORTUNITY TO DELIVER THIS

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:07.709
MESSAGE.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:13.114
HIS JOKE LATER WAS, HOW GREAT

00:01:07.842 --> 00:01:13.982
WAS IT TO HAVE LENIN BACK TO

00:01:13.247 --> 00:01:14.515
STARE AT MY BACKSIDE FOR AN HOUR

00:01:14.115 --> 00:01:16.918
AND A HALF?

00:01:14.649 --> 00:01:18.353
BUT IT TURNED OUT TO BE THE

00:01:17.185 --> 00:01:24.359
PERFECT FORUM FOR HIM TO DELIVER

00:01:18.486 --> 00:01:26.327
HIS MESSAGE.

00:01:24.492 --> 00:01:27.528
&gt;&gt; Bret: THE STUDENTS FILED IN

00:01:26.461 --> 00:01:28.930
AND SETTLE DOWN.

00:01:27.662 --> 00:01:30.798
HE WARMED UP HIS AUDIENCE BY

00:01:29.063 --> 00:01:32.567
WISHING THEM SUCCESS IN THEIR

00:01:30.932 --> 00:01:34.335
OWN LANGUAGE.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.137
&gt;&gt; I KNOW YOU MUST BE VERY BUSY

00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:36.738
THIS WEEK STUDYING AND TAKING

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:42.977
HER FINAL EXAMINATIONS.

00:01:36.871 --> 00:01:50.118
SO LET ME JUST SAY -- [SPEAKING

00:01:43.111 --> 00:01:52.487
IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

